A cast is dispatched on the declaration it resolves to, not on the name the
call site wrote.

`date`, `time` and `datetime` are stdlib structs in `sngl:time`, so a program
reaches them through a dot import (`date("2026-05-09")`) or through an alias
(`time.date("2026-05-09")`). Both name one StructDef, both are the same cast,
and both must therefore build the same `ir.Conversion` -- which is the node the
optimizer folds (`internal/optimize/consteval.go`, `evalConversion`).

The qualified spelling used to build an `ir.Call` with no `Func` instead,
because the bare path matched on the written identifier while the namespace
path had a special case only for units (`time.duration(1m)`). `isConstExpr`
answers false for such a call, so nothing folded: android emitted a runtime
constructor and html initialised the field to null and assigned at startup,
where the identical program written with a dot import got a literal. A
qualified import silently cost the program its constant folding.

The two components here are that program written both ways, so the golden shows
the two initialisers side by side on every target: `dotted` and `qualified`
must fold alike, field for field.

`color` is the fourth struct-backed cast and has no qualified spelling at all:
it lives in `sngl:builtin`, which is ambient and may not be imported, so there
is nothing to alias it as.

deny out/kotlin/android/MainScreen.kt `mutableStateOf\(time\.` -- the unfolded cast reached Compose as `mutableStateOf(time.date("2026-05-09"))`, a call to nothing Kotlin declares
deny out/none/html/index.html `__inst1: null` -- an unfoldable field is initialised to null and assigned at startup; a folded one is a literal in `state`
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `= time\(` -- the call kept only its receiver's alias, so Go got `m.d__inst1 = time("2026-05-09")` -- JS got the same, and crashed on load

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import . "sngl:time"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
    none {
        html
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

component dotted node {
    var d date = date("2026-05-09")
    var t time = time("14:30:00")
    var dt datetime = datetime("2026-05-09T14:30:00")

    text(value=string(d))
    text(value=string(t))
    text(value=string(dt))
}

window {
    dotted
    qualified
}
-- qualified.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import time "sngl:time"

component qualified node {
    var d time.date = time.date("2026-05-09")
    var t time.time = time.time("14:30:00")
    var dt time.datetime = time.datetime("2026-05-09T14:30:00")

    text(value=string(d))
    text(value=string(t))
    text(value=string(dt))
}
